@page
@model PrivacyModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}
<div class="tvdb-shell">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
        <div class="col-sm-10 col-md-8 col-lg-6">
            <h1 class="tvdb-display mb-3">@ViewData["Title"]</h1>

            <p class="tvdb-prose">
                Recall.nu is a TV and movie tracker. We collect the minimum needed to run your
                account — your email address and the shows, episodes and likes you add — and
                don't sell or share it with third parties.
            </p>

            <h2 id="cookies" class="h4 mt-4 tvdb-display">Cookies</h2>
            <p class="tvdb-prose">
                The site uses only cookies that are technically necessary for it to work — for
                example, keeping you signed in and protecting forms against abuse. No cookies are
                used for tracking, analytics or advertising, and we don't share any information
                with third parties for those purposes.
            </p>
            <p class="tvdb-prose">
                Because every cookie we set is necessary for the site's core functions, there's
                nothing to opt out of — no cookie preferences to manage.
            </p>

            <h2 class="h4 mt-4 tvdb-display">Sign-in</h2>
            <p class="tvdb-prose">
                Recall uses passwordless, email-based sign-in — there's no password to store.
                Sign-in requests are protected against automated abuse using Cloudflare Turnstile
                and volumetric rate limits.
            </p>

            <h2 class="h4 mt-4 tvdb-display">Logs</h2>
            <p class="tvdb-prose">
                The web server may temporarily log standard information such as IP address and
                browser type for operational and security purposes. Logs aren't used to profile
                individual visitors.
            </p>

            <h2 class="h4 mt-4 tvdb-display">Contact</h2>
            <p class="tvdb-prose">
                Questions about how the site handles your data? Get in touch and we'll be happy
                to help.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
